the reality is most of us could use a  little less screen time and a little  more face-to-face so today I'm gonna  give you 10 tips to put more life in  your living but first shout-out to Ahmed  who deleted all of his social media apps  and survived this video has two parts  first I'm going to share with you some  ways to help you ease into healthier  phone habits and at the end I'll share  some more challenging tips for those of  you who want to live on the wild side so  number one avoid using your cell phone  when you're sharing a meal with others I  mentioned in my videos six reasons why I  do not own a TV that my family has a  rule where we do not allow cell phone  use at the dinner table or really any  meal when we eat as a family we value  that time it's time to catch up share  ideas laugh and enjoy each other's  company  number two if you're eating out with  someone don't place your phone on the  table it subliminally sets a barrier  kind of like a message saying I'm  waiting for a call or I'm wanting to  check on something  it's like looking at your watch when  you're having a conversation you're done  yet  number three this is kind of a personal  one to me but please do not use your  phone at the register I used to be a  cashier and some people would be on  their phone the entire time some  wouldn't even say a single word to me  throughout the whole process not only is  that rude but all humans deserve respect  and dignity even cashiers so my tip for  this is if you're on the phone kindly  tell that person to wait just a moment  while you pay for something that way you  won't have to divide your attention  between two people and no one will get  hurt  and all of these three tips the main  takeaway is to be mindful of the people  in the world around you there is a world  outside your phone thanks for listening  to me  it's been really hard for me lately and  it's the first time that I've talked to  someone about it you're really sorry  were you talking to me I had my  headphones in tip number four no phones  on the bed don't allow yourself to use a  phone on the bed because you'll end up  checking on just one more thing and  you'll never go to sleep and also the  blue light emitted from your phone tells  your brain that it's daytime and it  makes it even harder for you to fall  asleep  even after turning your phone off and  number five when you actually go to bed  put distance between you and your phone  so that you actually have to physically  get out of bed to get to it this will  help you by placing a barrier to make it  less likely that you will actually get  up to go get it but an added bonus is if  it is your alarm clock it's also much  more likely that you're gonna get out of  bed shut that thing off and if after all  of this you still get out of bed to get  to your phone and check it in the middle  of the night consider putting a bedtime  alarm on it number six was a big one for  me turn off notifications five years ago  when I had social media this one was a  big one for me because I just had to  check that little message icon to see  what it was all about it is addicting it  releases dopamine which tells your brain  that it's pleasurable and so you need  more of this if you have trouble with  notifications turn them off it can help  easier temptation and tip number seven  okay this is a weird one but don't use  your cell phone in the bathroom I mean  can we not live without our phones for  just a few minutes what do you think  about this one okay so I shared seven  small changes with you now let's get to  the big stuff cold turkey style number  one delete social media I told you these  were a bit more challenging if you're  struggling to put your phone down  chances are social media might have  something to do with it if you need some  motivation as to why you should consider  quitting social media check out my video  six reasons why I quit social media  I haven't had social media in five years  and I don't need it you can survive and  thrive without it the next one  delete gaming apps that you spend the  most time on okay don't laugh but candy  crush was my addiction must crush  Candy's but seriously this game kept me  up at night because I just had to get to  the next level if this sounds like you  toss them you don't need them they're  depriving you of sleep and depriving you  of activities that could be a lot more  productive and more fulfilling and while  you're at it if you want even more of a  challenge then do like a spring cleaning  through all of your apps by asking  yourself if each one of them actually  brings value to your life or if it's  actually useful I mean is candy crush  really a necessity and the last one  replaced that extra time with something  that's more productive that brings you  joy my diet is much healthier than it  was 10 years ago  but it never felt like I was missing out  on anything because instead of focusing  on what I couldn't have I focused on  adding and having more of healthier  choices and the same applies to habits  in general when you miss mindlessly  scrolling through your phone or you're  bored and you're tempted to pull it out  just because have a list of things that  you can do instead that bring you joy  the point here is to trick your brain to  release that dopamine with other things  it can be exercised listening to music  or doing a hobby that you enjoy there  was a world before phones so be creative  and think of other activities that you  can do to replace that screen time but  be sure to share them in the comments so  that we can all learn from each other  and for sticking to the end my bonus tip  for you is beware of FOMO this is huge  when it comes to eliminating unhealthy  tech habits because billions of dollars  are invested into the production of  Bones apps and advertisements that are  meant to keep us glued I was asked what  if I missed an important phone call and  all I was doing was eating yummy cake  great question number one why should I  be concerned and not answering my phone  if it is a life and death call then I'm  probably not the person to call this  should probably be calling 9-1-1  and number two if it actually is that  important they would probably call more  than once and something you can do to  help you with this FOMO is to go ahead  and let your friends and family know  that during next time or ex activity you  won't be answering your phone  that way you won't be worried that  you're going to miss an emergency and  they won't be worried that something is  wrong and point number three my last one  for this question I work with dying  patients for a living and this has  changed my mentality in so many ways the  small details in life are worth enjoying  yes even a piece of yummy but  unnecessary cake if I'm gonna do  something enjoyable like eating cake I  want to do it mindfully and actually  enjoy it so long story short yeah I may  not answer my phone to eat some yummy  cake that's all for today guys if you  have your own ideas please share them in  the comments and if you like this video  don't forget to Like and subscribe so  that you won't miss out on my weekly  videos I thank you so much for watching  and I can't wait to see you in the next  one  [Music]  okay now I want something who's with me
 

